<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασκευ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>get ready, set in order,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				15.27.9
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				24.32
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>equip,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ βασιλικῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Nec.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς Σατύρους διεσκευασμένοι</span>
			<i>dressed</i> as . ., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλοις</span> Aen. Tact.<i><span class="en">
				26.1
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>prepare for oneself, provide,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἆλλα ὡς ἐς πλοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.38
				</span></i>
			; <i>arm, equip</i> or <i>prepare oneself,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς εἰς μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.2.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διεσκευάσθαι πρὸς τὸν δῆμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Din.
					1.70
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασκευάσασθαι πρὸς τοὺς δικαστάς</span>
			<i>prepare all one's tricks</i> for a trial, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				3.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασκευασάμενος τὴν οὐσίαν</span>
			<i>having disposed of one's</i> property, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				29.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>revise</i> or <i>edit</i> a work <i>for publication,</i>
			Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				311
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>compile,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ πολλῶν [βιβλίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>elaborate</i> with rhetorical devices, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτία μὲν κατασκευάζει, τρόπος δὲ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Inv.</u>
					2.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
